                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5749791f-2a4d-3550-a54c-950fde04d15f",
                        "entry_id": "b8e878ec-ed25-3507-9792-0f732be079f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To blossom more beautifully than, or with more flowers than."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "170db130-248a-4ba9-ae56-575663001389",
                                "sense_id": "5749791f-2a4d-3550-a54c-950fde04d15f",
                                "text": "Fifty a contemptible Age! Not at all, a very faſhionable Age I think—I aſſure you, I know very conſiderable Beaus, that ſet a good Face upon Fifty,. Fifty! I have ſeen Fifty in a ſide Box by Candle-light, out-bloſſom Five and Twenty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "993555b7-c1c5-40a5-b05b-9d41844c4843",
                                "sense_id": "5749791f-2a4d-3550-a54c-950fde04d15f",
                                "text": "True, one rose will outblossom the rest, one rose in a bower."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5c47a24-896c-4502-a14d-90865afb162c",
                                "sense_id": "5749791f-2a4d-3550-a54c-950fde04d15f",
                                "text": "For cars using artificial flowers, an Oldsmobile entered by the local agency was conceded to “outblossom” its rivals, the color scheme being purple and white, clematis blossoms being used to further the effect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21e9527c-ed76-49fd-8471-96a3a0368c2d",
                                "sense_id": "5749791f-2a4d-3550-a54c-950fde04d15f",
                                "text": "The nationwide spring, summer, and fall flower festivals are thought by many to outblossom those in Holland."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcd12492-c507-38c0-a47a-4c49b3b56f99",
                        "entry_id": "b8e878ec-ed25-3507-9792-0f732be079f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bloom in spite of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b55902ed-e4d2-4151-afa5-36820de4bdc8",
                                "sense_id": "bcd12492-c507-38c0-a47a-4c49b3b56f99",
                                "text": "I hear in her poems something that will outblossom hell itself and help us all to turn it back into earth again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cb07108-d970-438a-a22f-99cd3fe3ab78",
                                "sense_id": "bcd12492-c507-38c0-a47a-4c49b3b56f99",
                                "text": "For a mere $1.50 per word we will introduce you to our audience of 250,000 hardy perennials who survived the Reagan winter. Meet them as they prepare to outblossom Bush."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bbb5782-1392-4d5d-9adc-e1c42275968d",
                                "sense_id": "bcd12492-c507-38c0-a47a-4c49b3b56f99",
                                "text": "And the chosen helper, this splash of colour, will it outblossom the greyness of discord, the black of mourning and the white of restrained emptiness?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa4ff985-a0e5-458d-811c-68f3ff1a90cc",
                                "sense_id": "bcd12492-c507-38c0-a47a-4c49b3b56f99",
                                "text": "More than once she stopped to listen, in the hush of the timid south wind creeping through the dishevelled wood; and once, but only once, she was glad to see her first primrose and last, and stooped to pluck, but, on second thoughts, left it to outblossom her."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3b99dfd-9406-3589-a107-6f45f951ea2e",
                        "entry_id": "b8e878ec-ed25-3507-9792-0f732be079f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To blossom forth; to emerge into a state of blossoming; to flower."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef482f9b-fc84-46b7-a86b-cd2d1eacb5a1",
                                "sense_id": "a3b99dfd-9406-3589-a107-6f45f951ea2e",
                                "text": "Be strong! the wind to the shorn lamb is tempered; The way, though weary, teacheth to repose ; Life, though with bitter memories hampered, Will yet outblossom as the summer rose.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4e534bd-2646-4953-baa4-b455f079a592",
                                "sense_id": "a3b99dfd-9406-3589-a107-6f45f951ea2e",
                                "text": "I know not why I make this confession, unless it be that I want to tell you how lenient the sense of my own self-esteem makes me with persons whose conceit outblossoms into vanity and positive egotism ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5af80dce-1e81-466d-b178-146b310169a7",
                                "sense_id": "a3b99dfd-9406-3589-a107-6f45f951ea2e",
                                "text": "Carrol did not know, then, that it was the outblossoming of Mary's love nature that gave such charm to her life and presence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac513f28-1395-4a5d-8fe6-57b66cf1f2ad",
                                "sense_id": "a3b99dfd-9406-3589-a107-6f45f951ea2e",
                                "text": "Full many a time I've watched that star / Outblossom through the night's allure, / And wondered if its hearthstones far / Know love that will endure."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
